1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,632
In April, Malika starts a second website, just for wedding flowers.

2
00:00:04,682 --> 00:00:09,432
Her company is approved, so she expects it to take payments the moment it goes up.

3
00:00:09,482 --> 00:00:11,304
It does not.

4
00:00:11,354 --> 00:00:23,016
In Lesson 18, her company was switched on, and in Lesson 20, her team got their roles, and this lesson checks and switches on each website on its own, because each one is a different risk.

5
00:00:23,066 --> 00:00:30,984
If every website of an approved company could take payments the moment it was typed in, that company could add a copy of a famous brand's shop.

6
00:00:31,034 --> 00:00:33,792
Then all the bank's checks on the company would mean nothing.

7
00:00:33,842 --> 00:00:36,000
Malika opens Websites.

8
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:40,896
The page says each website that takes payments is checked and switched on by the bank.

9
00:00:40,946 --> 00:00:42,768
She clicks Add website.

10
00:00:42,818 --> 00:00:49,560
She gives it a name, the website's address, and return addresses on that same site, pressing Enter after each one.

11
00:00:49,610 --> 00:00:53,496
Each website is a sales point: one place where buyers pay.

12
00:00:53,546 --> 00:00:59,448
When a payment ends, the buyer is sent back to the shop, and where they go is the return address.

13
00:00:59,498 --> 00:01:03,600
Every return address must be secure, and on the website's own site.

14
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:07,080
I think this is the most underrated field in the whole form.

15
00:01:07,130 --> 00:01:13,656
Without that rule, a fraudster could use the bank's own payment page to send buyers to a fake thank-you page.

16
00:01:13,706 --> 00:01:17,784
Bekzod tests it: he tries a return address on somebody else's site.

17
00:01:17,834 --> 00:01:20,760
The server refuses it, and the screen shows why.

18
00:01:20,810 --> 00:01:24,384
Malika saves, and the page says the bank will check it.

19
00:01:24,434 --> 00:01:28,224
The new site starts as a draft, and a draft cannot take money.

20
00:01:28,274 --> 00:01:32,592
Return addresses can change only while the website is still a draft.

21
00:01:32,642 --> 00:01:36,744
At the bank, Dilnoza opens Malika's shop and the new website.

22
00:01:36,794 --> 00:01:42,288
A card at the top says "Before it takes payments", with a list of steps and how many are left.

23
00:01:42,338 --> 00:01:44,232
The Switch on button is grey.

24
00:01:44,282 --> 00:01:49,896
A line explains: switching on needs an active merchant, a passed check and chosen cards.

25
00:01:49,946 --> 00:01:54,936
Dilnoza looks at the site, clicks Record a check, chooses Passed, and saves.

26
00:01:54,986 --> 00:01:57,120
A failed check must say what is wrong.

27
00:01:57,170 --> 00:01:58,992
Then Deal terms.

28
00:01:59,042 --> 00:02:04,728
The deal says which cards the website takes, and it can say how much it may take per payment, and per day.

29
00:02:04,778 --> 00:02:06,600
She ticks one card.

30
00:02:06,650 --> 00:02:12,048
The boxes "Most per payment" and "Most per day" can stay empty, which means no limit.

31
00:02:12,098 --> 00:02:15,792
Three steps now show done, and the Switch on button lights up.

32
00:02:15,842 --> 00:02:17,664
One click.

33
00:02:17,714 --> 00:02:24,336
A warning appears: some cards still have no terminal or fee, and their payments are refused until they do.

34
00:02:24,386 --> 00:02:26,208
So Switch on is not the end.

35
00:02:26,258 --> 00:02:30,960
Each card still needs its own terminal and its own fee before its payments go through.

36
00:02:31,010 --> 00:02:37,848
And before taking any money, every part of the system asks one question: may this website take a payment right now?

37
00:02:37,898 --> 00:02:42,072
The answer is yes only when the website and its merchant are both active.

38
00:02:42,122 --> 00:02:46,560
Suspend either one, and payments stop at once, everywhere.

39
00:02:46,610 --> 00:02:51,744
The bank checked Malika's company once, and it still checks every website she opens.

40
00:02:51,794 --> 00:02:54,696
Next: how the bank's fee is decided.
